[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":113},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news-detail-auburn-university-scholarship-2026-in-usa-fully-funded-274":3},{"news":4,"more":30},{"id":5,"slug":6,"title":7,"content":8,"authorName":9,"authorId":10,"status":11,"recommended":12,"datePosted":13,"deadline":14,"images":15,"notifiedAt":14,"notifiedBy":14,"createdAt":13,"updatedAt":24,"categories":25,"readTime":27},274,"auburn-university-scholarship-2026-in-usa-fully-funded-274","Auburn University Scholarship 2026 In Usa | Fully Funded","\u003Cp>Auburn University is offering fully funded Master’s scholarships in the form of assistantships for home and foreign students.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>The Auburn University Scholarship covers tuition and provides a living stipend of $25,000 per year.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Auburn University Scholarship Abstract\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Scholarship Host: Auburn University\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Study Abroad: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarship\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study Abroad\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fcategory\u002Fscholarship\u002Fscholarships-in-usa\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study-In-USA\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Location: United States of America (USA)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Category: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> ||  \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fpostgraduate-scholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Postgraduate Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fmasters-scholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Masters Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Benefits: Full Scholarship\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Tuition\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>$25,000 Living Stipends\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Eligibility: All Countries\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Deadline: May 31, 2026\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Auburn University Masters Scholarship Details\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>Two MS assistantship positions are available starting May or September 2026 at Auburn University in collaboration with the Aquatic Reproductive Physiology lab (P.I. Dr. Ian A.E. Butts).\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>In these projects the students will develop intensive indoor rearing strategies for these species during the critical early life stages.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To accomplish this goal, the students will use basic and applied research to gain a better understanding of developmental, physiological, and behavioral functions associated with their development. Specific studies will focus on optimizing environmental factors (i.e., light, oxygen), tank design, and feeding conditions. \u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Auburn University Scholarship Benefits\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>The Auburn University Scholarship covers;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Full tuition fees\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>$25,000 annual living stipend\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Auburn University Scholarship Requirements\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To be eligible for the postgraduate Auburn University Scholarship, applicants must satisfy the following conditions:\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Bachelor’s degree in biology or similar discipline \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Knowledge of aquaculture and fish physiology  \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Proven ability to carry out goal-oriented work and fluent with data management systems (i.e., Excel, Word, statistical analysis)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Lab competences in molecular biology and\u002For physiology would be considered an asset – please clarify your experiences in the “motivating letter”\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Practical husbandry experiences with aquatic organisms will be an asset\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Good co-operation ability\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Required Documents\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>While applying for the Auburn University Scholarship, you will be required to submit the following documents;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Cover letter motivating the application (please include your background, interests, goals)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Curriculum vitae with contact information (e-mail and phone numbers) for three referees  \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Unofficial transcripts and GRE scores.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>How To Apply for Auburn University Scholarship 2026\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To apply for the Auburn University Scholarship, follow the instructions we have outlined below; \u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Read the information we have provided on this webpage and ensure your eligibility.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Email the following as a single PDF to Dr. Ian A.E. Butts at \u003Ca href=\"mailto:iab0007@auburn.edu\">iab0007@auburn.edu\u003C\u002Fa>.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Cover letter motivating the application (please include your background, interests, goals)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Curriculum vitae with contact information (e-mail and phone numbers) for three referees  \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Unofficial transcripts and GRE scores.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Please submit your application no later than \u003Cstrong>31 May 2026 at 11:59 PM CDT\u003C\u002Fstrong>.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>The students will begin coursework and research in Aug. 2026. \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Selected candidates will be contacted and notified.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>Begin your application by clicking on the button below.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>Deadline: May 31st, 2026\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>Apply here: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.gcub.org.br\u002Fdestaque\u002Ffifth-edition-of-the-gcub-international-mobility-program-gcub-mob-gcub-mob-call-for-applications-no-001-2026\u002F\">https:\u002F\u002Fwww.gcub.org.br\u002Fdestaque\u002Ffifth-edition-of-the-gcub-international-mobility-program-gcub-mob-gcub-mob-call-for-applications-no-001-2026\u002F\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>","Linkskool",16,"published",0,"2026-06-01 10:53:07",null,[16,21],{"fileName":17,"oldFileName":17,"type":18,"file":19,"url":20},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fauburn-university-scholarship-2026-in-usa-fully-funded\u002F6a1d5683c61ef9.47353785_screenshot 2026-06-01 104620.png","image","","https:\u002F\u002Flinkskool.com\u002Fassets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fauburn-university-scholarship-2026-in-usa-fully-funded\u002F6a1d5683c61ef9.47353785_screenshot%202026-06-01%20104620.png",{"fileName":22,"type":18,"file":19,"oldFileName":22,"url":23},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002F274\u002Fauburn-university-scholarship-2026-in-usa-fully-funded\u002F6a1d570fa15332.73936773_screenshot 2026-06-01 103804.png","https:\u002F\u002Flinkskool.com\u002Fassets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002